		(uuid "68cb9c91-be55-49d4-9716-2f3f615f8a25")
	)
	(text "shell pads G1-G4 to GND; card-detect switch A/B (closed with card) left open. Needs its own footprint on the PCB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 160.274 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6db354d0-6a90-4df0-bfef-24444d3910a3")
	)
	(text "2026-09-06: X3 is now the Hirose DM3D-SF push-pull socket (HRS 609-0025-8), DM3 catalog p9. Same 8-contact pinout;"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 157.734 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "93a868a1-a39f-4391-9c3e-d104fb0e972c")
	)
	(text_box "MASTER SPI BOOT (x4).  M2:M1:M0 = 0:0:1 -- R20 pulls M0 to VCC3V3, R21/R22 pull M1/M2 to GND -- so at power-up the FPGA \ndrives CCLK itself and clocks its bitstream out of U4 with no USB and no host present.  That mode can only use the dedicated \nconfiguration pins: CCLK C11, FCS_B K19, D00_MOSI D18, D01_DIN D19, D02 G18, D03 F18.  No other ball will do, which is why \nSDRAM A4 had to move off K19 (it is now on D17, still bank 14).  After DONE the six pins revert to ordinary user I/O. \nR2A/R2B keep WP#/HOLD# high through the x1 command phase and through the float window before the FPGA drives D02/D03 \n(PUDC_B is tied high, so the FPGA has no internal pull-ups).  R2D keeps FCS_B deselected. \nVivado:  set_property CONFIG_MODE SPIx4 [current_design]   set_property BITSTREAM.CONFIG.SPI_BUSWIDTH 4 [current_design] \nThe microSD is deliberately NOT on this bus any more: an inserted card sits in native SD mode watching bitstream traffic go \npast on what it believes is CMD, and one 48-bit window with a valid CRC7 is enough to make it answer and drive the line the \nFPGA is reading.  X3 now has its own CLK/CMD/DAT0 on R2/T1/T2, the bank-34 balls the flash just vacated, with R9 damping \nDAT0 where the socket stub is."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 185.939 37.592 0)
		(size -170.699 22.352)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3d996d03-0b12-4643-99af-60653c902a47")
	)
	(text_box "U3 DECOUPLING -- each cap bridges one supply pin to the ground pin OPPOSITE it. \nIn the 54-pin TSOP-II, pin n faces pin 55-n, and every supply pin faces a ground of its \nown domain: VDD 1/14/27 to VSS 54/41/28, VDDQ 3/9/43/49 to VSSQ 52/46/12/6. Alliance \nisolates VDDQ from VDD for DQ noise immunity -- LAYOUT MUST KEEP THE PAIRS: each cap on \nthe underside spanning its two pins, own vias, VDDQ returning to VSSQ and VDD to VSS. \nC10 is bulk and pairs with nothing. Do NOT split the ground plane."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 258.972 234.202 0)
		(size -120.172 12.192)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "44de6770-a85e-42a3-bbda-ef164a79b64b")
	)
	(text_box "U3 = AS4C32M16SB-7TCN: 512Mbit (32M x 16) = 64MB. \nPin-for-pin and dimensionally identical to the 256Mb \nAS4C16M16SA-6TIN it replaces -- all 54 pins and every \nTSOP-II dimension checked against both datasheets, and \npin 40 is NC on both. \nONE DIFFERENCE, AND IT IS NOT A PIN: the column address \nis A0-A9 (1024 columns), not A0-A8 (512).  The memory \ncontroller must be set to 10 column bits, or it reaches \nonly half the array.  Row A0-A12, banks BA0/BA1 and \nrefresh (8192 cycles / 64ms) are unchanged. \n-7TCN since 2026-09-08 (-6TIN dry): 143 MHz max at CL3,\ntRCD/tRP 21, tRC 63 ns, TA 0-70 C, IDD1 max 110 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 256.813 29.61 0)
		(size -76.473 24.384)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "856a9e76-1f4d-4ec8-bf33-f657f5d2c985")
	)
	(text_box "microSD runs the NATIVE 4-BIT SD BUS, not SPI.  CLK, CMD and DAT0-DAT3 -- six signals, all in \nbank 34 byte group T0 (R2 T1 T2 U1 V2 W2), so they can be constrained as one bus.  DAT1/DAT2 came \nfrom prototyping-header CHAN1/CHAN0; DAT3 is the old SPI chip-select, which needs no new pin. \nR34/R35 are the 4.7k pull-ups the SD spec requires on CMD and DAT0-DAT3.  R9 (100R on DAT0 \nonly) was removed: one damped line out of four is a skew, not termination."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 151.608 145.034 0)
		(size -133.828 10.16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "92b7749d-ac43-40dd-b98e-324645de7ef6")
	)
